igital Evidence'-'Generate Evidence Report' pairs can exist in a process instance, each adhering to this immediate succession rule. Events of 'Generate Evidence Report' can occur elsewhere in the process but not between an 'Analyze Digital Evidence' and its corresponding 'Generate Evidence Report'.\",\"template\":\"Chain Response\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Analyze Digital Evidence\",\"description\":\"The 'Analyze Digital Evidence' activity entails examining and interpreting digital evidence to extract relevant information for an investigation.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Generate Evidence Report\",\"description\":\"The 'Generate Evidence Report' activity entails creating a comprehensive report summarizing the findings from the analysis of digital evidence.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"If 'Secure Evidence Storage' activity occurs, then 'Validate Evidence Integrity' must also occur in the same process instance, and vice-versa. This mutual obligation ensures that neither event can occur without the other. The events can occur multiple times and in any order relative to each other. If neither event occurs, the constraint is still considered satisfied.\",\"template\":\"Co-Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Secure Evidence Storage\",\"description\":\"The 'Secure Evidence Storage' activity ensures that digital evidence is stored in a secure environment to prevent unauthorized access or tampering.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Validate Evidence Integrity\",\"description\":\"The 'Validate Evidence Integrity' activity involves verifying that digital evidence has not been altered or corrupted since its collection.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"A 'Report Security Breach' activity cannot be immediately followed by a 'Dispose Digital Evidence' activity; there must be at least one other event between them. Similarly, a 'Dispose Digital Evidence' event cannot be immediately preceded by a 'Report Security Breach' event. This constraint allows multiple occurrences of 'Report Security Breach' and 'Dispose Digital Evidence' in any order, provided they are not adjacent in the event sequence.\",\"template\":\"Not Chain Succession\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Report Security Breach\",\"description\":\"The 'Report Security Breach' activity entails documenting and notifying relevant parties about any security breaches that may compromise digital evidence.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Dispose Digital Evidence\",\"description\":\"The 'Dispose Digital Evidence' activity represents the secure and permanent disposal of digital evidence once it is no longer needed.\"},\"activation_condition\":null,\"correlation_condition\":null,\"time_condition\":null,\"cardinality\":null},{\"type\":\"binary\",\"description\":\"The 'Classify Digital Evidence' activity and the 'Dispose Digital Evidence' activity cannot both occur within the same process instance. This means that if 'Classify Digital Evidence' event occurs one or more times, 'Dispose Digital Evidence' must not occur at all in that process instance, and vice-versa. It is acceptable for neither event to occur. The constraint enforces a mutual exclusion between 'Classify Digital Evidence' and 'Dispose Digital Evidence', allowing for different process variants based on which event (if any) occurs.\",\"template\":\"Not Co-Existence\",\"activation\":{\"name\":\"Classify Digital Evidence\",\"description\":\"The 'Classify Digital Evidence' activity involves categorizing digital evidence based on its type, sensitivity, and relevance to the investigation.\"},\"target\":{\"name\":\"Dispose Digital Evidence\",\"description\":\"The 'Dispose Digital Evidence' activity represents the secure and permanent disposal of digital evidence once it is no longer needed.\"},\"activation_condition\":nul